-- its history table stays behind, so the same name cannot simply be registered again
SELECT paimon.add_table('pub_t'::regclass);                                    -- expect ERROR
ERROR:  paimon_slot: cannot replicate public.pub_t: Paimon table public.pub_t_hist is the retained history of public.pub_t, which stopped being replicated by remove_table
HINT:  a history table and its archives (pub_t_hist_<lsn>) are kept as the audit trail when their table is dropped or removed, and a new registration must not append to them. Rename or drop the Paimon table public.pub_t_hist and its archives by hand (from Spark or Flink, or move their directories), then run SELECT paimon.forget_history('public', 'pub_t_hist'); and add the table again
